  "notes": "Modified cash basis ESU (FY ended 8/31/2025); governmental funds statement (Exhibit III, p3) is a single General Fund column. Statement lines Local Receipts, Other Local Receipts, State Sources and Non-Revenue Receipts split using Schedule A account codes (p6); each split ties to the printed line. Tuition Receipts = 1380+1385+1395 (charges for services); Food Services = 1611+1620. ESU account-code rule applied: 1951/1960 -> intergovernmental/state aid (county/other local governments); nameplate capacity tax -> other taxes. Spending categories follow Exhibit III functions (Support Services lines tie to 21xx/22xx/23xx/25xx/26xx codes; Private & State Categorical and Federal Programs placed in instruction with review). Disbursement detail is by account code only, no object breakdown (not itemized). Blank-actual lines omitted (4105, 5301). Schedule A is the only fund schedule, no double counting. Balance sheet from Exhibit I (p1); Exhibit III p4 shows fund balance Assigned Employee Benefit 580,069.38, Assigned Depreciation 274,082.66, Unassigned 6,569,469.38. Identity: 6,656,990.73 + 10,639,824.55 - 9,873,193.86 = 7,423,621.42. v7 re-trim added p5 (report p18, Exhibit IV fiduciary custodial funds net position, 14,179.40 held for school districts): fiduciary, skipped, nothing added; Schedule A is now pp6-8. Read pages 1-8 of 8"
